# NetAtlas QX compatibility — optional; NOT LOSSLESS source-regex restoration.
# MIT; original adapter for the pinned MIT domain-list-community source expressions.
# Not included in default or standalone profiles; strict coverage remains 14/24.
# Exact source hostname expression, limited to visible HTTPS URLs.
# No DNS, UDP, arbitrary TCP, HTTP/3 or certificate-pinning coverage is claimed.
# Explicit HTTPS opt-in: enable MITM yourself and trust your own CA. No certificate is supplied.
# The MITM glob masks are broader than the reject expression; non-ad hosts can be decrypted.
^https:\/\/speed\.(coe|open)\.ad\.[a-z]{2,6}\.prod\.hosts\.ooklaserver\.net(?::0*(?:[0-9]{1,4}|[1-5][0-9]{4}|6[0-4][0-9]{3}|65[0-4][0-9]{2}|655[0-2][0-9]|6553[0-5]))?(?:[/?][^\s#]*)?(?![\s\S]) url reject

hostname = speed.coe.ad.??.prod.hosts.ooklaserver.net, speed.coe.ad.???.prod.hosts.ooklaserver.net, speed.coe.ad.????.prod.hosts.ooklaserver.net, speed.coe.ad.?????.prod.hosts.ooklaserver.net, speed.coe.ad.??????.prod.hosts.ooklaserver.net, speed.open.ad.??.prod.hosts.ooklaserver.net, speed.open.ad.???.prod.hosts.ooklaserver.net, speed.open.ad.????.prod.hosts.ooklaserver.net, speed.open.ad.?????.prod.hosts.ooklaserver.net, speed.open.ad.??????.prod.hosts.ooklaserver.net
